# Resenha
The running of many Lince in one computer. In the Resenha mode of Lince, as a TUI, you are able to:
- [ ] See all your Lince instances.
- [ ] Add Lince instances.
- [ ] Remove Lince instances.
- [ ] Update each instance separatelly or all at the same time, configuring:
	- [ ] Port of the application.
	- [ ] Directory it is running in.
	- [ ] Name of it's own Local Organ for recognizing in the network discovery.
	- [ ] Known Organs (contacts)
	- [ ] Sync settings between Organs
- [ ] Deterministic Simulation Testing: the runtime that with initial seeded data in possibly any table, random or specific, simulates time, disk and network. If the app is deterministic (and it should be) we should be able to put the same seed and run the Resenha of a Lince or several Lince instances through many years of automated interactions and whatnot, with availability of disk and network differing for writing and access tests, and have the same intended result, the same state in the end.
	- [ ] Time simulation 
	- [ ] Internal Network simulation:
		- [ ] Assigning ips in a created network.
		- [ ] Two instances inside different NATs, able to traverse it after being Known.
	- [ ] 
	- [ ] 
	- [ ] 


